.TH SEEKER 1 "November 2026" "Seeker 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
seeker \- fast desktop file search tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seeker
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFOLDER\fR...]
.br
.B seeker \-\-cli
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFOLDER\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seeker
finds files by name and by content. Without \fB\-\-cli\fR it opens a window,
with the form filled in from the options given. With \fB\-\-cli\fR it runs the
search in the terminal and prints the results.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIPATTERN\fR
File-name wildcards separated by semicolons, e.g. \fB"*.rs;*.toml;!*.lock"\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-name\-regex
Treat \fB\-\-name\fR as a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-text " " \fITEXT\fR
Text to find inside files.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-regex
Treat \fB\-\-text\fR as a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-case
Case-sensitive text search.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-word
Match whole words only.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hidden
Include hidden files and folders.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gitignore
Respect .gitignore and .ignore files.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-recurse
Do not search subfolders.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-follow
Follow symbolic links.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binary
Also search binary files.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " " \fILIST\fR
Folders to skip, separated by semicolons
(default: .git;node_modules;target;__pycache__).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-context " " \fIN\fR
Context lines shown in the preview.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-files\-only
In terminal mode, print only file paths.
.TP
.B \-\-auto
In the window, start searching immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Terminal mode; no window is opened.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
In terminal mode: 0 if something was found, 1 if nothing was found, 2 on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
seeker \-\-cli \-n "*.rs" \-t "fn main" ~/src
Find Rust files containing "fn main".
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/seeker
holds the window's saved settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rg (1),
.BR find (1)
